---
title: Guideline Record Template
description: Structured template for evidence-traceable architecture recommendations.
---

Use one file per guideline (`FE-###`). Do not publish a recommendation with missing evidence as established fact.

## Guideline ID

`FE-###`

## Title and short recommendation

_State one actionable recommendation, only when evidence supports it._

## Detailed explanation

_Define the context, intended audience, and behavior covered._

## Rationale

_Separate scientific rationale, empirical observation, and design judgment._

## Scientific evidence

_Cite verified source IDs, findings, experiment IDs, versions, dates, and limitations._

## Evidence scope and confidence

_State the population, system, outcome stage, and conditions supported. Explain directness, consistency, replication, and remaining uncertainty; distinguish evidence level from recommendation priority._

## Evidence level

_A/B/C/D with explicit justification; do not infer from an unverified claim._

## Priority

_Must / Should / Context-dependent; justify expected benefit, cost, and risk._

## Technology independence

_State invariant guidance; place framework-specific examples in a clearly supplementary section._

## Implementation guidance

_Provide actionable, accessible, framework-neutral guidance first._

## Validation method

_Specify a reproducible check and measurable outcome._

## Exceptions and trade-offs

_Describe cases where the recommendation may not apply and potential downsides._

## Related experiments, findings, and papers

_Link all related `EXP-###`, `FIND-###`, and verified `PAPER-###` records._
